  "id": "devcontainer-agent-toolchain",
  "generatedAt": "2026-10-08T03:24:49.723Z",
  "title": "Devcontainer agent toolchain and hook wiring",
  "summary": "This change turns the devcontainer image from a minimal Rust + moon box into a full factory workstation: it pins and checksum-verifies Node, pnpm, Bun, gh, actionlint, uv, moon and git-town; installs four coding agents (codex, claude-code, opencode, omp) plus dsh from its own lockfile; builds the repo's own dsh/omp/opencode integrations from the workspace pnpm lockfile; and wires every agent's hook files root-owned and read-only so `osf hook` runs on prompt and stop. The git wrapper now forces the hooks path per-invocation under OSF_WORKSPACE_ROOT instead of a system-wide core.hooksPath, and a battery of build-time tests proves the wrapper, hooks, toolchain read-only-ness and image cleanliness.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
